From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 19:34:58 +0200
Subject: phy: intel: grx500-usb: pass the chip-top offset as a syscon argument

The driver takes two properties to reach one register: intel,syscon for
the chip-top regmap and intel,syscon-offset for the byte offset of this
controller's AXI configuration word inside it. The offset is meaningless
without the phandle and the phandle is useless without the offset, so
splitting them lets a DT express half of the pair and get a probe
failure for it.

syscon_regmap_lookup_by_phandle_args() exists for exactly this shape and
has been in tree since 6.11. It parses the phandle and a caller-fixed
number of arguments in one call, so the pair collapses into

	intel,syscon = <&chiptop 0x34>;

The argument count belongs to the caller, not to the provider: the
helper uses of_parse_phandle_with_fixed_args(), so &chiptop needs
no #syscon-cells, and other references to it are unaffected by this
change. The PCIe PHY's zero-argument intel,syscon on the same node keeps
working and is deliberately left alone here -- it carries two shift
values that are not offsets into the syscon and would not collapse the
same way, and converting it is a separate change on a path this series
cannot retest.

The property has never been documented and nothing outside this tree
uses it, so there is no legacy form to keep parsing.

The DT half has to move in the same commit: the blob is built into the
kernel image on this platform, so a driver that reads one form and a
dtsi that spells the other never coexist in a bootable image.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-fable-5
Signed-off-by: Grische <github@grische.xyz>

diff --git a/arch/mips/boot/dts/intel-mips/xrx500.dtsi b/arch/mips/boot/dts/intel-mips/xrx500.dtsi
index 27011ed47f43..3c4d9d9673ad 100644
--- a/arch/mips/boot/dts/intel-mips/xrx500.dtsi
+++ b/arch/mips/boot/dts/intel-mips/xrx500.dtsi
@@ -401,8 +401,7 @@ usb1_phy: phy@1a600000 {
 		clocks = <&cgu GCLK_USB1>;
 		resets = <&rcu_reset1 5 5>;
 		reset-names = "phy";
-		intel,syscon = <&chiptop>;
-		intel,syscon-offset = <0x34>;
+		intel,syscon = <&chiptop 0x34>;
 		status = "disabled";
 	};
 
diff --git a/drivers/phy/intel/phy-intel-grx500-usb.c b/drivers/phy/intel/phy-intel-grx500-usb.c
index 2a845f28b7d5..75be8dd0128f 100644
--- a/drivers/phy/intel/phy-intel-grx500-usb.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/intel/phy-intel-grx500-usb.c
@@ -200,16 +200,13 @@ static int intel_usbphy_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 		return dev_err_probe(dev, PTR_ERR(priv->base),
 				     "failed to map the PHY registers\n");
 
-	priv->chiptop = syscon_regmap_lookup_by_phandle(np, "intel,syscon");
+	priv->chiptop = syscon_regmap_lookup_by_phandle_args(np, "intel,syscon",
+							     1,
+							     &priv->cfg_offset);
 	if (IS_ERR(priv->chiptop))
 		return dev_err_probe(dev, PTR_ERR(priv->chiptop),
 				     "failed to get the CHIPTOP syscon\n");
 
-	ret = device_property_read_u32(dev, "intel,syscon-offset",
-				       &priv->cfg_offset);
-	if (ret)
-		return dev_err_probe(dev, ret, "missing intel,syscon-offset\n");
-
 	priv->clk = devm_clk_get(dev, NULL);
 	if (IS_ERR(priv->clk))
 		return dev_err_probe(dev, PTR_ERR(priv->clk),
